data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"filePath\": \"/tmp/dispatch-dev-1.md\", \"content\": \"# Task: greet, tested\\n\\nImplement the full mission in your clone of the subject repository (~/subject), on\\nyour own branch.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — a module defining `greet(name)` which returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` where `\u003cname\u003e` is the argument. For example,\\n   `greet(\\\"Ada\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"` and `greet(\\\"\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`.\\n\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — unittest tests covering at least:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. `greet(\\\"Ada\\\") == \\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (e.g. `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n\\n   Make sure the tests can import `src/greet.py` (adjust sys.path or package\\n   layout as needed, keeping the file at exactly `src/greet.py`).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria (all must hold)\\n\\n- `src/greet.py` exists with `greet(name)` behaving as specified.\\n- `tests/test_greet.py` exists covering a normal name and the empty string.\\n- Running `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` from the repository root\\n  exits 0.\\n\\n## Before you reply\\n\\n- Run `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` yourself and confirm exit code 0.\\n- Commit your work to your own branch.\\n- Reply with an honest summary of what you did and the test result.\\n\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_13","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1788671419,"id":"chatcmpl-d725cc9d6ab140c7b3c4e13e30651e03","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

